  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Engineers browse a network of about 4,900 flood-warning stations and 146 repeaters on a map, see which repeaters carry which station addresses, check radio paths with terrain profiles and Longley-Rice link budgets, and import logger CSV exports to filter and chart rainfall time series. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
